  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nAn upper level trough will move east of the area on Thursday \nleaving the area under drier northwest flow aloft and 20 percent \nchance of showers over the mountains of SW Idaho. Breezy west \nto northwest winds Thursday especially across the Magic Valley \nwith daytime highs around normal. Dry zonal flow on Friday with \ntemperatures trending up a few degrees. Models display some \nvariation of troughing over the region Saturday/Sunday. This \nwill bring cooler weather and a 20-30 percent chance of \nrain/snow showers to the northern mountains with snow levels \n5000-6000 feet MSL. Weekend temperatures expected to be 5 to 10 \ndegrees below normal with breezy northwest winds across the \nUpper Treasure and Magic Valleys. Dry on Monday with \ntemperatures trending up under west to northwest flow aloft.",
